From c08bb6769320dfc9a7be3d3a41029114668bc9aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/26] [Diffusion] Causal denoising: clean-boundary session
 hooks for KV archive backends

CausalDMDDenoisingStage and LongLive2CausalDenoisingStage accept an attached
causal KV backend (set_causal_kv_backend; class default None):

- A request carrying a causal_kv_session handle opens a backend run that may
  install restored history (latents, RNG state, cache slots) and returns the
  number of leading blocks to skip.
- Only the clean context forward of a block opens a capture scope (per CFG
  stream); denoising-step forwards are never captured.
- After each block (and its scene-cut pinning) the run commits the block and
  may pause at that clean boundary; a paused request outputs the generated
  blocks only. Failures are reported to the run before re-raising.
- LongLive2's multi-shot RoPE offset is factored into
  _causal_rope_start_frame so captured chunks record the exact RoPE position.

Requests without a session handle, and stages without a backend, run the
unchanged dense path.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
